PostgreSQL assumed. Expand-only migration: adds columns, backfills, keeps them in sync via trigger. `full_name` is **not** dropped here; drop it in a later migration once the app reads and writes the new columns.

```sql
-- migrations/2026_11_24_split_full_name.sql
-- Idempotent: safe to run any number of times.

BEGIN;

-- 1. Expand schema
ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS first_name text;
ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS last_name  text;

-- 2. Split helper: trims, collapses whitespace, first token -> first_name, rest -> last_name
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION split_full_name(full text, OUT first text, OUT last text)
LANGUAGE sql IMMUTABLE AS $$
  SELECT
    substring(n FROM '^\S+'),
    NULLIF(substring(n FROM '^\S+\s+(.*)$'), '')
  FROM (SELECT regexp_replace(btrim(coalesce(full, '')), '\s+', ' ', 'g') AS n) s
$$;

-- 3. Backfill only rows not yet migrated (re-run touches nothing already done)
UPDATE users u
SET    first_name = s.first,
       last_name  = s.last
FROM   users x
CROSS  JOIN LATERAL split_full_name(x.full_name) s
WHERE  u.id = x.id
  AND  u.first_name IS NULL
  AND  u.last_name  IS NULL
  AND  nullif(btrim(u.full_name), '') IS NOT NULL;

-- 4. Keep new columns in sync while old app code still writes full_name
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION users_sync_name_parts() RETURNS trigger
LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $$
DECLARE s record;
BEGIN
  IF TG_OP = 'INSERT' AND (NEW.first_name IS NOT NULL OR NEW.last_name IS NOT NULL) THEN
    RETURN NEW;  -- new code supplied parts explicitly
  END IF;
  SELECT * INTO s FROM split_full_name(NEW.full_name);
  NEW.first_name := s.first;
  NEW.last_name  := s.last;
  RETURN NEW;
END $$;

CREATE OR REPLACE TRIGGER users_sync_name_parts   -- PG 14+
BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE OF full_name ON users
FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION users_sync_name_parts();

COMMIT;
```

Re-run safety: `IF NOT EXISTS` / `CREATE OR REPLACE` → no-op on schema; backfill `WHERE` skips already-split rows and never overwrites manual edits; whole thing in one transaction → partial failure rolls back.

Gotchas: name splitting is lossy ("Mary Ann Smith" → `Mary` / `Ann Smith`, mononyms → `last_name` NULL, family-name-first cultures wrong); review edge cases before contracting. Tables in the millions → run step 3 in batches (`AND u.id IN (SELECT id … LIMIT 10000)` in a loop outside the transaction) to avoid long locks and bloat. PG < 14 → replace step 4's last statement with `DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS …; CREATE TRIGGER …`.
